{"title":"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Breif_Solution_of_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Breif Solution of Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call a permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a25c2f9720d16d7ab307b6766d3539fad0a05b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" /> of the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a70dad169cdc39a470a08a8fee6f6643d42c1d72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, \\ldots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> <i>quasi-increasing</i> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94ee5eae1241c59277d40d20e9b94f140340c915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k \\leq a_{k+1} + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/602172a66eee6b552713dfc2a219050b8822e217.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq k \\leq n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />. For example, 53421 and 14253 are quasi-increasing permutations of the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/a/9faa9b63684d102b90b612f4f964224e5437ce30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, but 45123 is not. Find the number of quasi-increasing permutations of the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08d23c373b8da8697fb948115c11c783a8e8c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, \\ldots, 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The simple recurrence can be found.\n</p><p>When inserting an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> into a string with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e80c6b6a84ad4015ea436a915435d69edbdd96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> integers, we notice that the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> has 3 spots where it can go: before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e80c6b6a84ad4015ea436a915435d69edbdd96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/438ca8cfe4ef1f8af9be1b9ba6670a87cced8f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, and at the very end.\n</p><p>Ex. Inserting 4 into the string 123:\n4 can go before the 2 (1423), before the 3 (1243), and at the very end (1234).\n</p><p>Only the addition of the next number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, will change anything.\n</p><p>Thus the number of permutations with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> elements is three times the number of permutations with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> elements. \n</p><p>Start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> since all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> permutations work. And go up: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc31d9c331c517f8cdec6e16b3a275120163f96a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18, 54, 162, 486$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Thus for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f0f830b5b25ea929198068e407e8c9f62f56c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/850d5090d1627311feb4e9fa689e9566800b58a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2*3^5=\\boxed{486}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"23\" /> permutations.\n</p><p>When you are faced with a brain-fazing equation and combinatorics is part of the problem, use recursion! This same idea appeared on another AIME with an 8-box problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Breif_Solution_of_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Breif_Solution_of_Solution_1)\">Solution 2 (Breif Solution of Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Breif Solution of Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Now consider an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We need to attach it to a permutation of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. The integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> should be placed before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/9/ef9b02e32cfba0db0f9038a8d077596720f62e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> or it should be completely placed at the end of the permutation of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. Why? To satisfy the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94ee5eae1241c59277d40d20e9b94f140340c915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k \\leq a_{k+1} + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Consider a permutation of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We have the possible permutations as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e86458535f4abc97c8421ac8ff60e628ba8775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12, 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Now consider a permutation of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. By the above mentioned strategy, the possible permutations are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e0f8381c4d4d5629db5775312d52e033977ddd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$312, 132, 123$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" /> for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> case and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/190a149583ec8ea5a96083a2bfbc3644fe429c63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$231, 321, 213$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" /> for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> case.\n</p><p>Observed It?\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be the possible allowed permutations. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aedb41ff9938d00ea1adce19c8ef72f67383b9a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = 3 \\cdot f(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/0478720e3af73128fb5d75aeba9f8c3d35bfc892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Hence using the relation we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d98b109e7591ced43b45c9e361efff2161a35856.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{|c|c|} \\hline n &amp; f(n) \\\\ \\hline 2 &amp; 2 \\\\ 3 &amp; 6 \\\\ 4 &amp; 18 \\\\ 5 &amp; 54 \\\\ 6 &amp; 162 \\\\ 7 &amp; \\boxed{486} \\\\ \\hline \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"145\" />\n</p><p>If you are interested in a direct relation then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/051a4b565d46a39baed37dc57e6cbbb6ec90773d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=3^{n-2}\\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e55156a4008b0944ad00d5bc71bc5aa6315aabb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sim$\" style=\"vertical-align: 2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"5\" /> Hardik (BlueE65)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\">2006 AIME I Problem 11</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II\" title=\"2015 AIME II\">2015 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017052106\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 273/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1808/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 130/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7041/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.955      1 -total\n 58.49%    7.578      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.61%    5.131      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14136:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017052106 and revision id 282651. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}